<p><a class=cimage href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/2025-07-29-2.jpeg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/2025-07-29-2.jpeg" alt="" width="840" height="326" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-114995" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/2025-07-29-2.jpeg 1781w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/2025-07-29-2-300x117.jpeg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/2025-07-29-2-1024x398.jpeg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/2025-07-29-2-768x298.jpeg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/2025-07-29-2-1536x597.jpeg 1536w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>Have you noticed how crowd-sourced &#8220;genre&#8221; tags are kinda&#8230;.  a thing that exists?</p>
<p>That is, I <a href="https://github.com/larsmagne/bookiez.el/issues/3" data-cached-time="2025-07-29T18:21:42" data-cached-image="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/cache-2025-07-29-web-1.webp" onmouseenter="hoverLink(event)">got some feedback</a> on my <a href="https://github.com/larsmagne/bookiez.el">Emacs package for keeping track of your books</a>, and the suggestions were eminently reasonable, so now there&#8217;s more usage instructions on Microsoft Github and stuff.</p>
<p>But it was also suggested that it&#8217;d be useful to add support for genres, and I was doubtful.  I mean, people don&#8217;t have hundreds of thousands of books (except the ones that do), so what would the actual utility be?  And besides, adding genre markers yourself would be actual work, and that&#8217;s ewwww.  Work!  Yuck.</p>
<p>Alors, I remembered that Goodreads has crowdsourced genre tags, so I could just query them?  So:</p>
<p><a class=cimage href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/2025-07-29-3.jpeg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/2025-07-29-3.jpeg" alt="" width="821" height="338" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-114996" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/2025-07-29-3.jpeg 821w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/2025-07-29-3-300x124.jpeg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/2025-07-29-3-768x316.jpeg 768w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 821px) 100vw, 821px" /></a></p>
<p>And I don&#8217;t know whether that&#8217;s useful, but it&#8217;s kinda fun, eh?</p>
<p>However, these are crowdsourced, so:</p>
<p><a class=cimage href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/2025-07-29-4.jpeg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/2025-07-29-4.jpeg" alt="" width="577" height="1063" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-114997" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/2025-07-29-4.jpeg 577w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/2025-07-29-4-163x300.jpeg 163w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/2025-07-29-4-556x1024.jpeg 556w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 577px) 100vw, 577px" /></a></p>
<p>Eh.  Yeah, &#8220;Autistic Spectrum Disorder&#8221; is definitely a genre that exists.</p>
<p>I&#8217;ve tried to filter out most of the junk by just using the two first genre tags per book &#8212; and that helps a lot, but still&#8230;</p>
<p>In any case, you can edit the genres manually if it bothers you.  Or just ignore the genres, really.</p>
<p><a class=cimage href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/2025-07-29-5.jpeg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/2025-07-29-5.jpeg" alt="" width="840" height="334" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-115001" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/2025-07-29-5.jpeg 1405w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/2025-07-29-5-300x120.jpeg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/2025-07-29-5-1024x408.jpeg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/2025-07-29-5-768x306.jpeg 768w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>Anyway, you can now list books based on genre, and&#8230;</p>
<p><a class=cimage href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/2025-07-29-6.jpeg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/2025-07-29-6.jpeg" alt="" width="796" height="1134" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-115002" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/2025-07-29-6.jpeg 796w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/2025-07-29-6-211x300.jpeg 211w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/2025-07-29-6-719x1024.jpeg 719w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/2025-07-29-6-768x1094.jpeg 768w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 796px) 100vw, 796px" /></a></p>
<p>&#8230; I&#8217;ve also fixed up how book details are displayed.</p>
<p>And I&#8217;ve also changed the data format from a very, er, &#8220;ad hoc format&#8221; is perhaps putting it too gently&#8230;  to JSON:</p>
<p><a class=cimage href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/2025-07-29-7.jpeg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/2025-07-29-7.jpeg" alt="" width="840" height="265" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-115003" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/2025-07-29-7.jpeg 1406w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/2025-07-29-7-300x95.jpeg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/2025-07-29-7-1024x323.jpeg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/2025-07-29-7-768x243.jpeg 768w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>So that should make it easier to import into other programmes, and also allow extending the format gracefully.</p>
<p><a class=cimage href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/2025-07-29-8.jpeg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/2025-07-29-8.jpeg" alt="" width="840" height="639" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-115004" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/2025-07-29-8.jpeg 945w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/2025-07-29-8-300x228.jpeg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/2025-07-29-8-768x584.jpeg 768w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>And there&#8217;s, of course, support for using barcode scanners, but I&#8217;ve extended that with a kinda &#8220;serverish&#8221; mode, so that you don&#8217;t have to select Emacs (or a bookiez mode) before scanning.  Just pick up the scanner and *beep*.</p>
<p>So there you go.  I think bookiez might actually be usable now&#8230;  perhaps.</p>
